A||||6||REDHOTT88||dipstick loose..||||1||
Z||000000||REDHOTT88||11-16-2001||04:23 PM||||My dipstick is real loose. Any easy way to fix? Can it be done without removing hood?||||reg||1
Z||000001||avengador1||11-16-2001||04:46 PM||||If you have a V-6, it should have a bolt that holds it to the bracket thats goes over the valve cover closest to the passenger compartment. If this bolt fell out, the dipstick tube could come out of its hole in the engine block. If the bolt is lost you could replace it with a sheet metal bolt no longer than 1/2 inch( or it will hit the valve cover). You can also apply some silicone adhesive near the base of the tube to help hold it in and seal it, but make sure you don't put any near the opening of the tube. Put it on the shoulder that stops the tube from going all the way down. Hope this helps. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||REDHOTT88||11-16-2001||04:52 PM||||Yes it is a V6, can I access this from the top or from under car?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Voytek||11-16-2001||06:20 PM||||From under the car is definitely easier.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/voyteks_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||avengador1||11-16-2001||06:24 PM||||Yes, under night be the best.||||reg||1
